    <h3>Security, Insurance, Compliance Overhead</h3>
    <p>These costs are non-negotiable and often underestimated by first-time operators:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Commercial cannabis insurance:</strong> $2,000-$4,000/month depending on coverage limits</li>
      <li><strong>Security system monitoring:</strong> $400-$800/month (required by OCP)</li>
      <li><strong>METRC seed-to-sale tracking:</strong> $600-$1,200/month for software plus staff time</li>
      <li><strong>Compliance audits and legal:</strong> $500-$1,500/month on average</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h3>The 280E Tax Burden — Your Biggest Expense</h3>
    <div class="callout-box warning">
      <div class="callout-icon">◆</div>
      <div class="callout-content">
        <strong>The IRS 280E Reality</strong>
        <p>Because cannabis remains Schedule I at the federal level, you cannot take standard business deductions. Normal expenses like rent, marketing, and general admin are not deductible. Your effective tax rate ends up 21-30% of gross profit rather than the standard 15-21% C-corp rate. Work with a cannabis-specialized CPA from day one — the 280E optimization strategies are real and meaningful.</p>
